# Zod Schema Rules

These rules follow the Zod 4 changelog: https://zod.dev/v4/changelog

## Avoid Deprecated Chained Validators

- Use Zod v4 top-level string format validators instead of deprecated chained string validators.
- Prefer:
  - `z.url()` instead of `z.string().url()`
  - `z.email()` instead of `z.string().email()`
  - `z.uuid()` instead of `z.string().uuid()`
  - `z.iso.datetime()` instead of `z.string().datetime()`
- Prefer the direct top-level validator, for example `z.url({ error: "URL must be valid." })`.

## Prefer Zod 4 Number Helpers

- Use `z.int()` instead of `z.number().int()` for integer fields.

## Avoid Deprecated Object Mode Helpers

- Use Zod v4 object constructors or object mode methods instead of deprecated object helpers.
- Prefer:
  - `z.looseObject({ ... })` instead of `z.object({ ... }).passthrough()`
  - `z.strictObject({ ... })` instead of `z.object({ ... }).strict()`
  - default `z.object({ ... })` behavior instead of `z.object({ ... }).strip()`

## Error Customization

- Use the unified Zod 4 `{ error: "..." }` parameter instead of deprecated message-style parameters.
- Example: `z.string().min(1, { error: "Required." })`.

## ZodError Reporting

- Use `error.issues` instead of deprecated `error.flatten()` or `error.format()`.
- Example: `JSON.stringify(parsed.error.issues)`.

## New Schemas

- Do not add new usage of deprecated Zod APIs.
- When touching an existing schema, modernize deprecated Zod usage in the edited area.
